# 3D Models

This directory contains STL files for 3D printing the voice satellite enclosure.

## Files

- **pokrywa.stl** - Top cover/lid
- **maskownica.stl** - Speaker grille
- **glosnik.stl** - Speaker mount/holder

## Printing Settings

### Recommended Settings
- **Layer Height:** 0.2mm
- **Infill:** 20%
- **Material:** PLA or PETG
- **Supports:** Not required
- **Brim/Raft:** Optional (depends on bed adhesion)

### Print Time
Approximately 4-6 hours total for all parts (on standard 0.4mm nozzle printer).

## Assembly

1. Print all three parts
2. Install WS2812B LED ring inside the lid (`pokrywa.stl`)
3. Mount MAX98357A speaker in holder (`glosnik.stl`)
4. Attach speaker grille (`maskownica.stl`)
5. Route cables through designated channels
6. Secure ESP32-S3 board inside enclosure

